  "nl_text": "The database name is rschema_0245, and it consists of five tables: User, Novel, Bookshelf, Book_review, and Novel_added_to_Bookshelf. The User table contains information about users, including their email, password, username, and creation and update times. The Novel table contains information about novels, including their title, description, author, ISBN, publication date, and creation and update times. The Bookshelf table contains information about bookshelves, including the user who created it, the novel it contains, and the time it was added. The Book_review table contains information about book reviews, including the user who wrote it, the novel it is about, the rating, and the review content. The Novel_added_to_Bookshelf table contains information about which novels have been added to which bookshelves, including the time they were added. Each table has a primary key, and there are foreign key constraints between the tables to ensure referential integrity.",
  "gold_question": "System Requirements Function Description\n\nAccording to the provided file content, Weishu is a novel reading system based on WeChat applet, and the main functional modules are as follows:\n\n1: My bookshelf: Users can add their favorite novels to the bookshelf for subsequent reading.\n\n2: Bookstore: Provides browsing and search functions for various novels, and users can find their favorite novels.\n\n3: Personal Center: Users can view and manage personal information, such as changing passwords, viewing bookshelves, etc.\n\n4: H5 reader: Provides online reading function and supports reading novel content directly in WeChat applet.\n\n5: Login and registration: Users can manage their accounts through registration and login functions.\n\n6: Book reviews: Users can comment on novels and share their reading experience.\n\n7: Book rankings: Display popular novel rankings to help users discover popular books.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0245.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0245\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `novel` (\n  `novel_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `author` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `isbn` varchar(13) NOT NULL,\n  `publication_date` date NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`novel_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `bookshelf` (\n  `bookshelf_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `novel_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `added_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`bookshelf_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `bookshelf_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `bookshelf_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`novel_id`) REFERENCES `novel` (`novel_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `book_review` (\n  `review_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `novel_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `rating` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `review_content` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`review_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `book_review_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `book_review_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`novel_id`) REFERENCES `novel` (`novel_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `novel_added_to_bookshelf` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `bookshelf_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `novel_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `added_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `novel_added_to_bookshelf_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`bookshelf_id`) REFERENCES `bookshelf` (`bookshelf_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `novel_added_to_bookshelf_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`novel_id`) REFERENCES `novel` (`novel_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
